{"name":"Beach Lilac","hex":"#bda2c4","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"},{"term":"lilac","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large shrub of the genus Syringa, especially Syringa vulgaris, bearing white, pale-pink, or purple flowers.","A flower of the lilac shrub."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Of a cat or its fur: having a pale brown colour, lighter than chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lilac"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach","wikidata":"Q40080"},{"title":"Syringa","blocks":[{"text":"Syringa is a genus of 12 currently recognized species of flowering woody plants in the olive family known colloquially as lilacs. They are native to woodland and scrub from southeastern Europe to eastern Asia, and widely and commonly cultivated in temperate areas elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syringa","wikidata":"Q157449"},{"title":"Lilac (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lilac is a light shade of purple or violet representing the average color of most lilac flowers. The colors of some lilac flowers may be equivalent to the colors shown below as pale lilac, rich lilac, or deep lilac. However, there are other lilac flowers that are colored red-violet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilac_(color)","wikidata":"Q12894641"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/1280px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg/500px-Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg/1280px-Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg/500px-Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMan_o'war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Beach_zones.png/500px-Beach_zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Beach_zones.png/500px-Beach_zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A berm is a nearly horizontal portion that stays dry except during extremely high tides and storms. The swash zone is alternately covered and exposed by wave run-up. The beach face is the sloping section below the berm that is exposed to the swash of the waves. The wrack line (not shown here) is the highest reach of the daily tide where organic and inorganic debris is deposited by wave action. May have sand dunes.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeach_zones.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Summer_versus_winter_beach.png/500px-Summer_versus_winter_beach.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Summer_versus_winter_beach.png/500px-Summer_versus_winter_beach.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The differences between summer and winter on beaches in areas where the winter conditions are rougher and waves have a shorter wavelength but higher energy. In winter, sand from the beach is stored offshore.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASummer_versus_winter_beach.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg/500px-Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut